  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-15" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;6. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-16" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-17" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;8. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-18" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;9. On December 1, 2025, Alliance Pipeline L.P. filed a rate case under Section 4 of the Natural Gas Act. A procedural schedule has been established, with an initial decision due May 26, 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:4.11pt"&gt;10. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="f-20" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:4.11pt"&gt;11. Pursuant to note 9, on December 31, 2025, FERC issued an order accepting and suspending the filed tariff records for five months, to be effective upon motion June 1, 2026, subject to refund. Alliance's actual recourse rate revenues will be subject to the final outcome of the pending proceeding in Docket No RP26-257-000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-21" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:4.11pt"&gt;12. Effective May 2, 2025, the following changes were made for Alliance Pipeline Inc., the general partner of Alliance Pipeline L.P:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Directors removed: Andrew Schwerha and Heather Christie Burns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Director added: Christopher S. Scherman&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Officer removed: Kelly Siemens, Chief Financial Officer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Officer added: Jason Metcalf, Vice-President, General Counsel &amp;amp; Corporate Secretary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Officer title change: Tanya Yeast's title changed from Vice-President to Vice-President, Tax.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Effective December 31, 2025, Janet C. Loduca resigned as a director of Alliance Pipeline Inc., the general partner of Alliance Pipeline L.P.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-22" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:4.11pt"&gt;13. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:18pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Notes to the Financial&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:18pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;(thousands&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;U.S.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;dollars,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;unless&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;otherwise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#005197;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;noted)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:17pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;General Business Description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance Pipeline L.P. (&#8220;Alliance&#8221; or the "Partnership") was formed under the laws of the State of Delaware on May 10, 1996. Alliance is wholly owned by Pembina Pipeline Corporation ("Pembina") indirectly through its affiliates and is managed by Alliance Pipeline Inc. (the "General Partner"). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;On April 1, 2024, Alliance acquired Enbridge Inc.'s ownership interest in Alliance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The General Partner&#8217;s sole activity is managing the business and affairs of Alliance. The rights, powers, duties, and obligations of the Managing General Partner are set out in Alliance&#8217;s Second Amended and Restated Limited Partnership Agreement (&#8220;Limited Partnership Agreement&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance owns and operates the United States (&#8220;U.S.&#8221;) portion of a 2,392 mile high-pressure natural gas transmission pipeline and related infrastructure and an 80 mile Tioga lateral and related infrastructure. The Canadian portion is owned by Alliance Pipeline Limited Partnership (&#8220;Alliance Canada&#8221;). Alliance and Alliance Canada have entered into contracts with shippers to transport natural gas from supply areas primarily in Northwest Alberta and Northeast British Columbia portions of the Western Canadian Sedimentary Basin and the Williston Basin in North Dakota to delivery points primarily near Chicago, Illinois. The pipeline connects in the Chicago area with five interstate natural gas pipelines and two local natural gas distribution systems, which provide shippers with access to natural gas markets in the Midwest, Northeast and Gulf Coast of the United States and Eastern Canada. Alliance&#8217;s pipeline operations are regulated by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:17pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Summary of Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:14pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The financial statements of Alliance have been prepared by management, as detailed in the accounting policies set out below, in accordance with accounting practices prescribed by FERC as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts. All dollar amounts stated in the Notes to Financial Statements are in thousands of U.S. dollars, unless otherwise noted. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;In management&#8217;s opinion, the financial statements have been properly prepared within reasonable limits of materiality and within the framework of the significant accounting policies. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:14pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Use of Estimates and Judgments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The preparation of the financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect both the amount and timing of recognition of assets, liabilities, revenues and expenses since the determination of these items may be dependent on future events. Management uses the most current information available and exercises careful judgment in making these estimates and assumptions. Actual results may differ from these estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Judgments, estimates and underlying assumptions are reviewed on an ongoing basis. Revisions to accounting estimates are recognized in the period in which the estimates are revised and in any future periods affected.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance recognizes revenue equal to the consideration the Partnership expects to be entitled to for satisfying a performance obligation to transfer control over a service to a customer. Alliance applies judgment when identifying performance obligations in contracts and determining whether each product or service promised to a customer is distinct and constitutes a separate performance obligation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The differences in timing of revenue recognition, reimbursements, and cash collections may result in recognition of invoiced receivables, unbilled receivables, contract assets, and contract liabilities. Amounts are invoiced in accordance with the contractual terms on a monthly basis or upon achievement of contractual milestones. Generally, billing occurs subsequent to the recognition of revenue, resulting in receivables from contracts with customers. Under some contracts, Alliance receives advances from customers which are recognized as contract liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance disaggregates its revenue streams based on the certainty of the associated cash flows to be received from the customer. Information about the nature of the services provided, consideration received, and timing of the satisfaction of performance obligations for each category is discussed below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Service Revenue from Related Parties&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The Executive, Managerial and Administrative service agreement (&#8220;EMA&#8221;) allows Alliance and Alliance Canada, an entity related by virtue of common ownership, to allocate shared services in exchange for reimbursement of incurred costs plus the applicable mark-up. Services allocated to Alliance Canada are invoiced in U.S. dollars on a monthly basis and revenue is recognized over time, using the input method based on the costs incurred to date, as administrative services performance obligations are rendered.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The entire consideration under the EMA is variable. The majority of the variability in the transaction price is resolved as the services are provided. The remainder of the consideration is estimated using a single most likely amount based on the projected cost and historical data.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Firm Transportation Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Firm transportation services are offered to shippers on a take-or-pay basis. The performance obligation is met when firm transportation services are made available to shippers during the contract period. The transaction price includes a demand charge, which is a fixed take-or-pay charge and usage charges, which are variable consideration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Firm transportation services revenue is recognized over the term of the contract, using an output measure of progress, as transportation services are made available to shippers. The fixed consideration is recognized in revenue as the service is made available to the shippers. The variable consideration is recognized in revenue as the actual volume of natural gas is transported.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance refunds the consideration received during a qualifying outage through a reservation charge credit. The refund liability is measured at the amount of consideration received from shippers where the service was not available due to the qualifying outage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Rich gas credits are considered variable consideration as they fluctuate in response to the gas composition and volumes transported. Rich gas credits are estimated using a single most likely amount based on historical data. The variability in the consideration is resolved one quarter after the service is provided based on the composition and volume of gas transported during the period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Interruptible Transportation Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Interruptible transportation (&#8220;IT&#8221;) services are offered on a daily basis. The entire performance obligation is satisfied by the end of each day based on the actual volume of natural gas that is transported. Revenue is recognized as shippers utilize the services. The entire transaction price is variable in nature as it is based on the actual volumes of natural gas transported.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Transportation revenues from IT services are recognized in a manner consistent with the underlying shipper agreements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Ancillary Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Ancillary services include term park and loan services. Shippers have the option to either store gas or borrow gas from Alliance. All of the revenue from term park and loan services is recognized over time, using an output measure of progress, as services are rendered. Alliance recognizes revenue based on the actual quantities of gas parked or loaned. The uncertainty related to the amount of consideration is resolved as the service is provided to the customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Ancillary services also include interruptible wheeling services, which are a transfer of gas between interconnecting pipelines. Revenue is recognized as customers utilize the services. The entire transaction price is fixed, and the charge is based on the terms stated in the contract.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Natural Gas Sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Revenue is recognized at a point in time when the title and control of gas is transferred to the customer. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Other Revenue &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Other revenue includes revenue from construction contracts and other contracts with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Under construction contracts, Alliance builds interconnection facilities to provide customers access to Alliance&#8217;s pipeline. Revenue from construction contracts, where Alliance has title to the constructed asset, is recognized over the term of the related firm transportation contract or over a specified period of time when there is no firm transportation agreement in place. Where the customer has title to the constructed asset, revenue is recognized upon completion of the constructed asset.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Inventory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Inventory is measured at the lower of cost and net realizable value and consist primarily of materials and supplies, including natural gas or operational line pack, and spare parts that are expected to be used within one year of the financial reporting date. Inventory cost is determined using the weighted average costing method and includes direct purchase costs. Materials and supplies are periodically reviewed for physical deterioration and obsolescence. All changes in the measurement of inventory is reflected in earnings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Financial Instruments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Financial assets and liabilities are offset and the net amount presented in the Statements of Financial Position when, and only when, Alliance has a legal right to offset the amounts and intends either to settle on a net basis or to realize the asset and settle the liability simultaneously.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Non-Derivative Financial Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance initially recognizes trade receivables and cash deposits on the date that they are originated. All other financial assets are recognized on the trade date at which Alliance becomes a party to the contractual provisions of the instrument. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Non-Derivative Financial Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance's non-derivative financial liabilities are comprised of trade payables and accrued liabilities, due to related parties, and other liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance initially recognizes non-derivative financial liabilities at fair value, plus any directly attributable transaction costs, on the trade date at which Alliance becomes a party to the contractual provisions of the instrument. After initial recognition, these financial liabilities are measured at amortized cost using the effective interest method. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Helvetica',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance derecognizes a financial liability when its contractual obligations are discharged, cancelled, or expire. On derecognition, the difference between the carrying value of the financial liability and the consideration paid, including any non-cash assets transferred or liabilities assumed, is recognized in earnings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Pipeline in Service Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Pipeline in service assets are recorded at cost and are depreciated on a straight-line basis over the estimated useful lives of the assets, commencing from the in service date. Estimated useful lives are based on the average service life of the asset. Costs are recognized as property, plant, and equipment if it is probable that future economic benefits will be realized, and the cost can be reliably measured. Major overhaul costs are capitalized and depreciated over their respective estimated service lives. Routine repairs and maintenance and other costs not meeting the capitalization criteria are expensed when incurred. Pipeline in service assets include the pipeline, compressor stations, meter stations, capital line pack and other related assets used to provide transmission services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Other Assets &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;General plant assets consist of field offices and ancillary equipment. These assets are recognized at cost and are depreciated on a straight-line basis over the useful lives of the assets, commencing when the asset is placed in service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;A provision for asset retirement obligation (&#8220;ARO&#8221;) associated with the retirement of Alliance&#8217;s property, plant and equipment has not been recognized in these financial statements. Alliance's ARO is considered indeterminate because there is no data or information that can be derived from past practice, industry practice, or management intentions to enable the Partnership to reasonably estimate the timing and scope of pipeline retirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Impairment of Non-Financial Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance's non-financial assets, such as property, plant and equipment, are assessed at each reporting date to determine whether there is any indication of impairment. If any such indication exists, the total of the estimated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;undiscounted future cash flows from use of the asset, or the estimated selling price of the long-lived assets, are compared to the carrying value of the asset. If the expected cashflows are sale price are less than the carrying amount, an impairment loss is recognized for the excess of the carrying value over the estimated fair value of the asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;These estimates and assumptions are susceptible to change and may differ from actual future developments. This estimation uncertainty could impact quantified recoverable values and, therefore, any related impairment charges, which may be material.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Impairment losses are recognized in earnings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:174%"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;Alliance is not a taxable entity for federal and state income tax purposes. In accordance with FERC requirements, the accompanying financial statements reflect income taxes as if Alliance was a corporation. Deferred taxes are recognized for temporary differences between the relevant basis of the assets and liabilities for financial reporting and tax purposes. The impact of changes in tax legislation on deferred income tax liabilities and assets is recorded in the period of enactment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:174%"&gt;The current tax liability or asset recognized each year in accordance with FERC requirements is relieved through proprietary capital in the current period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAssetsRetirementObligationsAROTextBlock id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#00497f;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:17pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:67.352%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:6.786%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:6.786%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:6.786%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:6.790%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="background-color:#00497f;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="background-color:#00497f;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Pipeline in service assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1,955,886&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,944,113&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;General plant and administrative assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;10,355&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;10,305&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Assets under construction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;8,120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#00497f;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="5" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,862&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Right of use assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;